# Line endings, pinned so every clone agrees (copied from methodica-math-ratio-01).
#
# Every text blob in the index is already LF (`git ls-files --eol`: 40 i/lf, 0 i/crlf),
# so this renormalises nothing in history. `eol=lf` additionally pins the WORKING TREE
# to LF on Windows, where core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check out CRLF. Packages are
# assembled from the working tree, so this is what makes them byte-identical to their
# commit whoever builds them (Documentation/reporting-and-resume §11.1).

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary, so auto-detection is never the only thing guarding media.
*.ttf   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.docx  binary

# SVG is XML — text, never binary.
*.svg   text eol=lf
